1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:08,200
That was leaving properly. Readmission is the return from an approved leave.

2
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:20,800
Therese Lacson, a student already on approved leave, signs in.

3
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:35,399
The Readmission page says Therese is on leave and enrollment stays closed until readmission is approved. The leave being ended is pre-filled.

4
00:00:36,399 --> 00:00:45,199
The rule: a returning student writes an intent to enroll, Handbook page fifty-three.

5
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:02,399
Therese picks the return semester, gives a reason for returning, and confirms the four checklist items.

6
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:09,899
Again, a summary to check first.

7
00:01:10,099 --> 00:01:19,099
Submitted. The request goes to Graduate School staff, then to the Dean.

8
00:01:19,299 --> 00:01:25,899
Graduate School staff signs in.

9
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:37,200
The Readmission board: same layout, own columns. Therese's card is in Submitted.

10
00:01:40,299 --> 00:01:44,000
Graduate School staff drags it to review.

11
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:53,299
The request shows the return semester, the intention, and the linked leave.

12
00:01:53,500 --> 00:02:07,299
The checklist shows what the student ticked, not yet verified. Below, the history: one year in the program, two of four leave semesters already approved.

13
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:20,000
The policy check flags an early return, before the leave ends. Only the Dean can allow that, so it shows Needs review.

14
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:40,400
Forwarding, Graduate School staff ticks the items verified. Anything unticked reaches the Dean as Needs review.

15
00:02:40,599 --> 00:02:45,300
Forwarded, locked, waiting for the Dean.

16
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:52,000
The Dean signs in to decide.

17
00:02:57,300 --> 00:03:09,700
The Dean finds Therese's request in With the Dean.

18
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:19,400
The Dean approves it, back in the program, with a note.

19
00:03:19,599 --> 00:03:30,700
Therese is active again. Readmission restores standing but does not enroll the student in subjects. The Academic Coordinator does that next.

20
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:43,800
Graduate School staff signs in.

21
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:54,900
The staff board now shows the Academic Coordinator as next owner, flagged for the Registrar.

22
00:03:55,099 --> 00:04:02,300
Same Registrar list: Graduate School staff downloads, sends, marks sent, then acknowledged.

23
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:18,000
Finally, Therese signs back in.

24
00:04:18,199 --> 00:04:26,100
Therese sees the approval, with messages from staff and the Dean.
